(DATA RETENTION AND PRIVACY POLICY - SPAIN) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Meridian Logistics Group - Corporate Compliance Series, Document CP-ES-403) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Purpose and Scope) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This policy defines how Meridian Logistics Group collects, stores, retains and deletes) Tj T*
(personal and business records within its Spain operations. It applies to all employees,) Tj T*
(contractors and third-party processors handling data on behalf of the company in Spain. The) Tj T*
(policy exists to ensure lawful processing, to limit storage to what is necessary, and to) Tj T*
(guarantee that records are disposed of securely at the end of their lifecycle.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Definitions) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Personal data means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural) Tj T*
(person. Business records include contracts, invoices, correspondence, audit trails and) Tj T*
(operational logs produced in the course of business. A data breach is any security incident) Tj T*
(leading to accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration or unauthorized disclosure) Tj T*
(of data.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Key Compliance Facts - Spain) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Customer records retention period: 6 years from the end of the business relationship.) Tj T*
(Supervisory authority: the Agencia Espanola de Proteccion de Datos \(AEPD\). Maximum fine for) Tj T*
(non-compliance: EUR 10 million. Data breach notification deadline: 96 hours after becoming) Tj T*
(aware of the breach. Appointed Data Protection Officer: Carlos Ortega. Annual policy review) Tj T*
(month: November.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Storage and Security) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All records must be stored on approved company systems with access restricted on a need-to-) Tj T*
(know basis. Encryption at rest and in transit is mandatory for personal data. Backup copies) Tj T*
(follow the same retention limits as primary records and are verified quarterly by the) Tj T*
(infrastructure team.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Deletion Procedure) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When the retention period defined in section 3 expires, records are deleted during the) Tj T*
(monthly disposal window. Deletion requests are logged, and a certificate of destruction is) Tj T*
(produced for physical media. Exceptions require written approval from the Data Protection) Tj T*
(Officer and must reference an active legal hold.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Breach Response) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Suspected breaches must be reported to the security desk immediately. The Data Protection) Tj T*
(Officer assesses severity and notifies the supervisory authority named in section 3 within) Tj T*
ET
endstream
